From 4d0a5611931ea54ad9628f0dd9dd35b90883e7f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:39:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 310/314] gallium/pvr: integers, honest formats, varying
 subsets, HWRT data set cache

- Advertise native integers: the state tracker stored int uniforms as
  floats while pco read them as integers, so a loop bounded by uniform
  int 1 ran 0x3f800000 times and hung the geometry data master
  (glmark2 loop).
- is_format_supported answers per binding with what the draw path can use
  (textures with a texture-state layout, RGBA8/BGRA8/X render targets,
  depth formats, float32 vertex attributes), so the state tracker
  converts RGB8 textures and integer attributes instead of passing
  formats the draw then rejects. RGBX8/BGRX8/R8 textures added.
- A fragment shader may read fewer components of a varying slot than the
  vertex shader writes (stages are compiled apart); iterate those.
- HWRT data sets are cached by target size (4, least recently used freed
  with DESTROY_HWRT_DATASET and their buffers), each with its own local
  free list as the reference. One leaked per size change exhausted the
  firmware (CREATE_HWRT_DATASET: ENOSPC) and every later draw fell back.

glmark2-es2 off-screen now runs every default scene on the 3D path except
depth-texture and unbound-sampler draws; score 410 (synchronous submits).
